class:: Limcycle
summary:: Generalized self-limiting relaxation oscillator
related:: Classes/Oscnet, Classes/Fracflight
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic

description::

A self-oscillating nonlinear ODE integrated per sample with RK4. It grows out of the
Van der Pol limit cycle but adds two morphs the textbook oscillator lacks, plus a
stochastic forcing path that ties it to Tether's stochastic family:

list::
## code::shape:: morphs the nonlinear damping from position-based (0, Van der Pol —
sine to relaxation buzz) to velocity-based (1, Rayleigh — a different asymmetry).
## code::well:: morphs the restoring force from a single well (0) to a double well
(1, Duffing) where the rest point at 0 becomes unstable and the state flips between two
basins — a route to chaos even without forcing.
## code::noise:: injects heavy-tailed (Lévy) kicks (shaped by code::tail::, like
link::Classes/Fracflight::) so the limit cycle is jostled by rare large impulses;
near a bifurcation this produces stochastic mode-switching and coherence resonance.
::

Two outputs: code::[position x, velocity x']::. Pitch tracks code::freq:: exactly only
near code::mu = 0::; the period stretches as code::mu:: and code::well:: rise.

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: freq
Natural frequency (Hz). Default 110.
argument:: mu
Nonlinearity / damping, 0–50. ~0 sine, higher = relaxation. Default 1.
argument:: shape
Damping morph: 0 Van der Pol (1-x^2), 1 Rayleigh (1-(x'/w)^2). Default 0.
argument:: well
Potential morph: 0 single well, 1 double well (Duffing). Default 0.
argument:: force
Amplitude of the sinusoidal forcing term. Default 0.
argument:: forceFreq
Frequency of the forcing term (Hz). Default 55.
argument:: noise
Amount of heavy-tailed stochastic forcing. Default 0.
argument:: tail
Lévy stability index for the noise, 0.5–2. 2 = Gaussian, lower = heavier tails. Default 2.
argument:: oversample
Integration sub-steps per sample, 1–32. Raise for stability at high code::mu::/code::freq::. Default 4.
argument:: mul
argument:: add

examples::
code::
// mu as waveshaper: mu~0 is a sine; raising it bends the cycle into a relaxation wave.
{ Limcycle.ar(110, MouseX.kr(0.05, 12), oversample: 16)[0] * 0.3 ! 2 }.play;

// shape morph: same energy, different asymmetry as damping shifts Van der Pol -> Rayleigh.
{ Limcycle.ar(110, 6, MouseX.kr(0, 1), oversample: 16)[0] * 0.3 ! 2 }.play;

// double-well chaos: push well up and the state flips between two basins, no forcing needed.
{ Limcycle.ar(90, 4, 0, MouseX.kr(0, 1), oversample: 16)[0] * 0.3 ! 2 }.play;

// stochastic kicks: heavy-tailed forcing jostles the cycle; lower tail = rarer, bigger jumps.
{ Limcycle.ar(110, 3, 0, 0.2, 0, 55, MouseX.kr(0, 400), MouseY.kr(2, 0.6), 16)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

// forced -> chaos: strong sinusoidal forcing period-doubles into chaos.
{ Limcycle.ar(80, 5, 0, 0, MouseX.kr(0, 8000), 120, 0, 2, 12)[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;
::
